module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.body_type_annotation_dropped_before_resolve_in_v2

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data body_type_annotation_dropped_before_resolve_in_v2: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "body_type_annotation_dropped_before_resolve_in_v2" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**a type written inside a fn body never reaches v2 resolve, so a type name nothing declares is accepted there** (INVALID STATE: v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold lowers `let y: T = e` to Bind[binder, value, body] with the annotation not carried, and preserves a fn literal `fn(y) -> T { .. }` as a structure shell (body_lower_is_structure_preserved_emitted) whose return type no resolve arm reads. So the type expression is dropped before the reference-site collector sees it.)",
    "HARM, OBSERVED BY EXECUTION (crisp-dove-95, 2026-09-24, locally built gunbc over v2.compiler.program_assembly assemble_program_from_ingest, head 748535dabe1): `fn f<T>(x: T) -> T { let y: Q = x; y }` and `fn f<T>(x: T) -> T { let g = fn(y) -> Q { y }; x }` are both ACCEPTED with `Q` declared nowhere -- silent wrongness, outside the ladder. The same bodies with `T` are accepted too, but for the same wrong reason: nothing resolved the annotation. The cast `x as Q` accepts likewise; that route is rostered separately as gunbc.recurring_failure_mode as_cast_has_no_lowered_form and is not claimed here.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Not gunbc.recurring_failure_mode generic_type_parameter_resolved_as_an_ordinary_atom_in_v2: that class is a type position that IS resolved against the wrong scope; here the position is never resolved at all, so no frame -- including that row's trigger (2), a position-aware body type frame -- can answer in it. The recognition rule: a type expression inside a v2-lowered Arrow body that has no counterpart in the lowered tree resolve walks, or one present only inside a preserved production shell no resolve arm reads.",
    "WORSE ON THE FN-LITERAL ROUTE, MEASURED THE SAME WAY: a let-bound fn literal `let g = fn(y) -> Q { y }` lowers to Bind[g, Atom(dag_token_kw_fn), ..] -- v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_bound_value's operand arm descends into the literal's shell and returns its first token, so the WHOLE literal (parameters, return annotation, body) is dropped, not only its annotation. As a call argument the same literal refuses body_lowering_reason_call_argument_unread, which is loud and honest.",
    "CLIMB, LET ANNOTATION (crisp-dove-95, step (0) of neat-boar-16's ordering): the statement-form let annotation now REFUSES body_lowering_reason_type_annotation_not_carried, located at the annotation (v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_let_annotation_optional), instead of being dropped. Control v2.test.claim.body_type_annotation_refusal btar_let_annotation_refuses, red before (Accepted), with its unannotated twin btar_unannotated_let_accepts. This takes the let route from outside the ladder to rung 1 (a typed, located refusal) and costs no new model. WHAT IT NEWLY REFUSES, DECLARED: every annotated statement let on the v2 body-lowering route, including CORRECT ones whose type is declared -- no rung is lowered (the previous state was a silent accept, outside the ladder), but v2-route acceptance of those correct programs is withdrawn. POPULATION: the modules matched by `git grep -lE` for an indented `let NAME :` over *.dag -- 75 files at gunbc#12248's base, listed by name on that PR; the one non-test v2 module among them is v2.compiler.test_marker_capture. Measured by execution on gunbc#12248: the required lanes (floor, witnesses) and both self-host instruments (emit-build: //gunbc/instruments:self-host and :v2-native-cli) are green with the refusal in place, so no population the required gate compiles on the v2 route contains one. Out-of-gate v2-route readers of the live tree (long claims, gunbc.tools.body_lowering_population_probe) may now report these files refused, which is the honest reading. RESTORATION TRIGGER: a v2.std.node carrier on Bind for the let annotation, read by resolve in a type role -- SUFFICIENT FOR every annotated let in that population lowering with its annotation resolved, so the refusal is deleted, not narrowed.",
    "CLIMB, FN-LITERAL ROUTE (crisp-dove-95, side-chat REQUEST_CHANGES on gunbc#12248, overriding the earlier deferral to gunbc#12210 -- a deferred silent accept is what DESIGN section 5 forbids). Two edits. (i) v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_bound_value refuses a fn literal's return annotation body_lowering_reason_type_annotation_not_carried at the authored type expression BEFORE the operand arm sees the literal. The grammar admits no other annotation on a function literal: fn-literal parameters and arrow-lambda parameters are bare identifiers (dag_grammar_untyped_params_helper, dag_grammar_arrow_lambda_expr). (ii) The eraser itself: body_lower_try_operand_or_reject's first-atom fallback answered a shell with its first atom, so a literal lowered to Atom(dag_token_kw_fn) wherever that fallback ran (a let value, an if arm); body_lower_atom_is_keyword_token now declines a lexer keyword token there, so every probed position -- let value, if arm, fn-body tail, match arm, record field, data initializer -- refuses loudly instead of accepting. The unannotated let-bound literal's disposition CHANGES on purpose: Accepted-by-erasure before, a loud resolve refusal now. Controls v2.test.claim.body_type_annotation_refusal btar_fn_literal_return_annotation_refuses (exact reason, locus = authored Q), btar_unannotated_fn_literal_is_not_erased, btar_if_arm_fn_literal_is_not_erased; the let row btar_let_annotation_refuses asserts the locus too, and anchoring that refusal at the surrounding let reds it (mutation receipt).",
    "RUNG, PER PATH, revised after the required floor passed on gunbc#12248 head d2d840af222 (all five checks green). Let annotation: mitigatable (rung 1) -- a typed refusal at the authored type (btar_let_annotation_refuses, locus asserted). Fn-literal return annotation: rung 1 the same way (btar_fn_literal_return_annotation_refuses). The erased literal itself, on the let-value and if-arm routes: a loud refusal now (btar_unannotated_fn_literal_is_not_erased, btar_if_arm_fn_literal_is_not_erased); the other probed positions -- fn-body tail, match arm, record field, data initializer -- refuse at resolve. No probed path accepts silently; the cast route is rostered separately (as_cast_has_no_lowered_form). THE CLASS'S CURRENT RUNG IS RUNG 1, MITIGATABLE, the minimum across those paths. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a body type position lowers to a carried type expression resolve walks in a type role. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, each naming a capability: (a) a v2.std.node carrier on Bind for the let annotation, read by resolve in a type role; (b) gunbc#12210 lowering function values in value position to Arrows carrying their written return type, walked by v2.compiler.resolve resolve_arrow_node, which replaces the fn-literal refusal with a resolved annotation. Either lands the first body type position, the trigger for the position-aware frame named by generic_type_parameter_resolved_as_an_ordinary_atom_in_v2.",
    "CLIMB, LET ANNOTATION, TRIGGER (a) FIRED (proud-cat-604, 2026-09-25, item 2a): the let annotation is now CARRIED, not refused. v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_let_annotation_lowered lowers it as a type expression onto its Bind as the v2.std.type_binder <type-annotation> edge (v2.std.compilers.body_lowering lower_bind_annotated; at most one Named edge beside the three positionals, v2.std.node PositionalPlusOneNamedEdges); v2.compiler.resolve resolve_bind_edges resolves it through resolve_type_role_target, so `let y: Q = x` refuses resolve_reason_unbound_symbol located at Q (btar_let_annotation_refuses, re-pointed), a body annotation `T` binds the fn's <T> and a type parameter in value position refuses located (v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation); v2.compiler.infer infer_bind_annotation_check refuses a bound value that does not inhabit the annotation. The let route is therefore at the class ceiling, structurally guaranteed. The class minimum stays rung 1 while the fn-literal return route refuses (trigger (b), gunbc#12210). Retires gunbc.rung_drop typed_statement_let_refuses_until_the_bind_annotation_carrier.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_let_annotation_optional", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_let_annotation_lowered", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation", decl_name: "bla_generic_annotation_binds_the_type_parameter", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_bound_value", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_type_annotation_refusal", decl_name: "btar_let_annotation_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_type_annotation_refusal", decl_name: "btar_fn_literal_return_annotation_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_atom_is_keyword_token", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_is_structure_preserved_emitted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.resolve", decl_name: "resolve_arrow_node", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
